{
  "title": "Pakjesavond",
  "goal": "Describe activities in progress with aan het, bezig zijn met, and positional verbs + te.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 1
      },
      "content": "Pakjesavond",
      "id": "40cbfba3-f7f3-43ef-9c47-3eaee86473ca"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It is Saturday 5 December, and Noor's flat is full of friends. They are celebrating Sinterklaas together. In this lesson you will describe activities as they happen, ask what people are busy with, and use zitten, staan, liggen or lopen with te. Verbs are blue; time is orange; place is purple.",
      "id": "dcec7353-9065-446d-8320-d8d00347c53c"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Story: around the table",
      "id": "910c9d85-a04e-4eb8-8407-9ad3a186ea4d"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "props": {
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Wat gezellig! Wie is er aan het voorlezen?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Daan",
            "text": "Ik zit Sofia’s Sinterklaasgedicht voor te lezen."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "En? Is het grappig?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Daan",
            "text": "Ja! En ik zit erin met een fiets van karton."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Fleur",
            "text": "Daan, ben je aan het raden?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Daan",
            "text": "Nee, ik ben niet aan het raden. Ik weet het!"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Fleur, ben jij bezig met je pakje?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Fleur",
            "text": "Ja, ik ben bezig met mijn pakje."
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "448e9ef4-ffd0-4a16-8ad6-0086dcef66a6"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "bezig",
              "meaning": "busy",
              "example": "Fleur is bezig. ",
              "id": "8bf5d906-b335-4889-b099-1ab0e4053464"
            },
            {
              "term": "bezig zijn met",
              "meaning": "to be busy with",
              "example": "Ik ben bezig met mijn pakje.",
              "id": "26de7b57-5a95-460c-9822-7d11f389e8fb"
            },
            {
              "term": "voorlezen",
              "meaning": "to read aloud (separable)",
              "forms": "leest voor · las voor · voorgelezen",
              "example": "Daan leest het gedicht voor.",
              "id": "fc199713-3ccf-45f3-afd0-301015a669f6"
            },
            {
              "term": "raden",
              "meaning": "to guess",
              "forms": "raadt · raadde/ried · geraden",
              "example": "Daan raadt het niet.",
              "id": "6c07ca78-ab6e-41d4-9f0c-2aeb009e8687"
            },
            {
              "term": "lachen",
              "meaning": "to laugh",
              "forms": "lacht · lachte · gelachen",
              "example": "Iedereen lacht.",
              "id": "cb9b3880-1542-4e38-8288-da9e8852dd4c"
            },
            {
              "term": "het Sinterklaasgedicht",
              "meaning": "poem for pakjesavond",
              "forms": "de Sinterklaasgedichten",
              "example": "Daan leest haar Sinterklaasgedicht voor.",
              "id": "35293bd9-ade3-4649-ad42-f56956bc39d9"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "76758a0d-c15a-4c28-b8f5-37edab79f84d"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "grammar",
        "icon": "book-open"
      },
      "content": "Use zijn + aan het + infinitive for an activity in progress. Put niet before aan het: Ik ben niet aan het raden.",
      "id": "be5703cc-105e-46d8-bd59-05207d19b5df"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Ik",
        {
          "text": "ben",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " aan het luisteren."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "I am listening.",
        "note": "The activity is happening now."
      },
      "id": "f37da771-56ec-4f96-9124-24f21521b92e"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Daan",
        {
          "text": "is",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " zijn gedicht aan het voorlezen."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Daan is reading his poem aloud.",
        "note": "The object comes before aan het; keep the separable infinitive together."
      },
      "id": "e74b578e-fb29-4562-ac61-e5ca6ff3d718"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Wie",
        {
          "text": "is",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " er aan het voorlezen?"
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Who is reading aloud?",
        "note": "A question about the activity now."
      },
      "id": "755393d0-390a-4a0e-a3e2-a7e7f73e8b43"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Wat",
        {
          "text": "zijn",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " jullie aan het doen?"
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "What are you doing?",
        "note": "Recycles the fixed question from 22-a."
      },
      "id": "060b510c-78c4-46e4-9655-560406a67496"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "We gaan zo uitpakken.",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "We are going to open the gifts in a moment.",
        "note": "For a plan, use gaan + infinitive, not aan het."
      },
      "id": "5e324b9f-30bc-4feb-b314-657a972859d0"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "uitpakken",
              "meaning": "to unwrap (separable)",
              "forms": "pakt uit · pakte uit · uitgepakt",
              "example": "We gaan zo uitpakken.",
              "id": "90bf0916-dcbd-49db-acea-75db2cf019c9"
            },
            {
              "term": "Van wie is dit?",
              "meaning": "Whose is this?",
              "example": "Van wie is dit pakje?",
              "id": "584aebee-bf94-4b47-bc25-09fd3762c934"
            },
            {
              "term": "Wat is er aan de hand?",
              "meaning": "What is going on?",
              "example": "Wat is er aan de hand?",
              "id": "ccd59c6f-292f-4458-a207-9445a2894b98"
            },
            {
              "term": "Wat grappig!",
              "meaning": "How funny!",
              "example": "Wat grappig!",
              "id": "601a697f-4db1-4235-a445-d9bfc790d654"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "aa510e09-d83c-43a9-b56b-d9fdaeea8c5e"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "important",
        "icon": "star"
      },
      "content": "Three descriptions: Ik ben aan het lezen (activity); Ik zit te lezen (position plus activity); Ik ben bezig met mijn gedicht (busy with a noun).",
      "id": "d2a83c93-3716-455d-b68a-b02a468ed6c6"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "culture",
        "icon": "globe"
      },
      "content": "At pakjesavond, adults often read poems and open handmade surprises. People may guess who made each surprise.",
      "id": "81c01825-106e-46a2-bb85-869de3a2e803"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Een Sinterklaasgedicht heeft vaak rijm. Daan leest een regel voor.",
      "id": "30154f3d-1d8a-4d73-b58e-5f4c16f2a267"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "het rijm",
              "meaning": "rhyme",
              "example": "Het rijm in het gedicht is grappig.",
              "id": "321e507f-a914-48ef-b2cb-0e28037c4ae6"
            },
            {
              "term": "de regel",
              "meaning": "line (of a text)",
              "forms": "de regels",
              "example": "Daan leest een regel voor.",
              "id": "a6dd7037-35bd-468a-adea-887a346f7bc0"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "6a7ce50f-8a84-4f8b-835f-ae5f8c9964dd"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Three ways to describe an activity",
      "id": "4f8a54c8-93d6-4853-9e04-ea4356c98b40"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "Position plus te",
      "id": "0827faf5-2d3d-475d-b23a-8113ca3a5b49"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Sitting, standing, lying or walking can show the person’s position while an activity happens. Put te before the infinitive. With a separable verb, te goes between the prefix and verb.",
      "id": "e0f4e2ef-14e6-47c6-87eb-c7fad43e088e"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "grammar",
        "icon": "book-open"
      },
      "content": "zitten / staan / liggen / lopen + … + te + infinitive. Example: Daan zit zijn gedicht voor te lezen. The infinitive with te comes last.",
      "id": "ec73fe92-a335-4796-be0f-c2facd7aedfd"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Fleur",
        {
          "text": "staat",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " in de keuken te koken."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Fleur is standing in the kitchen cooking.",
        "note": "The standing position is clear and relevant."
      },
      "id": "06465d5c-cf20-4a15-b8ac-d657a64213c7"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Tijger",
        {
          "text": "ligt",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " te slapen."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Tijger is lying down asleep.",
        "note": "Storyline fact: Henk’s cat is at home; this is a lesson example."
      },
      "id": "f66cefc5-7baf-4329-83eb-f3c5355c7b48"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Sofia",
        {
          "text": "zit",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " een berichtje te schrijven."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Sofia is sitting and writing a message.",
        "note": "The object comes before te."
      },
      "id": "adc2873b-2bdd-4fde-b9db-0ba0c210dfd3"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Daan",
        {
          "text": "zit",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " het pakje uit te pakken."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Daan is sitting and unwrapping the gift.",
        "note": "Separable uitpakken: uit + te + pakken."
      },
      "id": "3db18194-d81d-477d-898f-c1e05a4454f1"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Sofia",
        {
          "text": "staat",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " thee te maken."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Sofia is standing and making tea.",
        "note": "te goes before the infinitive."
      },
      "id": "2828ed7b-8eee-49fd-80e1-60d726533875"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        "Sofia ",
        {
          "text": "loopt",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        " te zingen."
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "Sofia is walking around singing.",
        "note": "lopen + te + infinitive; lopen describes movement during the activity."
      },
      "id": "59cfafc1-a9a8-4b66-9d10-05e0f9a71481"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        "Common mistake: ",
        {
          "text": "Daan zit te voorlezen.",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true,
            "backgroundColor": "gray"
          }
        },
        " → Daan zit voor te lezen."
      ],
      "id": "59a05b21-c16a-4f39-8210-2c66307c01a4"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "warning",
        "icon": "triangle-alert"
      },
      "content": "With a separable verb, put te between the prefix and the verb: *zit te uitpakken* → zit uit te pakken.",
      "id": "ec88e833-2db8-442d-8f52-fa2e38087ccd"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Bezig zijn met takes a noun: Ik ben bezig met mijn surprise. Use aan het for an activity when the position is not important. Use zitten, staan, liggen or lopen + te when position or movement matters.",
      "id": "967288b4-25b2-4a28-b9a8-d41f032d46ed"
    },
